cmu-wendigo-lab-paper-content =
    {"[color=#7a1f1f]⬢[/color] [head=2]Weyland-Yutani Biological Research Division[/head] [color=#7a1f1f]⬢[/color]"}
    {"[color=#7a1f1f]▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬[/color]"}
    {"[bold]PROJECT MH. CLEARANCE 3. EYES ONLY.[/bold]"}

    Your laboratory has been cleared to continue Project MH. MH-32 is available through your ASRS terminal under Research. Stock is limited and slow to restock: do not waste it.

    {"[head=3]1. Candidate selection[/head]"}
    • A living, unaugmented human. Synthetics and non-human candidates do not respond.
    • The candidate must be starving when the trial begins.
    • Candidates with a prior appetite for human flesh produce markedly superior results.

    {"[head=3]2. Materials and compound preparation[/head]"}
    • Two portions of [bold]raw human tissue[/bold] and one entire [bold]raw human heart[/bold]. Partial or cooked portions do not count. The final feeding must be a heart.
    • [bold]MH neural primer[/bold]: 5u Alkysine, 5u Gold, 5u Sugar. Heat to at least 370 K and mix. Yields 15u.
    • [bold]Stabilized Mutagen[/bold]: 10u Dylovene, 5u Uranium, 1u Gold, 5u Unstable Mutagen. Chill to 270 K or below and mix. Yields 15u.
      Unstable Mutagen: 1u Chlorine, 1u Radium, 1u Phosphorus. Yields 3u.
    • [bold]Brain treatment[/bold]: reserve additional Alkysine or prepare for brain surgery. Mutagen damages the brain; restore it to Bruised or better before the heart feeding.
    • [bold]MH tissue stabilizer[/bold]: 5u Cryoxadone, 5u Dylovene, 5u Platinum. Chill to 270 K or below and mix. Yields 15u.
    • [bold]MH-32[/bold]: ASRS, Research category.
    • [bold]MH-33[/bold] (conditioned compound): 15u MH-32, 15u Gold, 10u Platinum, 32u Black Sludge. Chill to 270 K or below and mix. Yields 15u.
      Black Sludge: 16u each of Bicaridine, Meralyne, Kelotane and Dermaline. Yields 64u.
    • Mix compounds using a closed chemistry container. Experimental compounds are administered by injection only, in [bold]full 15-unit doses[/bold]. Prepare separate doses and check injector settings.

    {"[head=3]3. Procedure[/head]"}
    1. Have the starving candidate finish the first raw tissue portion.
    2. Once reactive, have the candidate finish the second raw tissue portion.
    3. Once reactive again, inject MH neural primer.
    4. Inject Stabilized Mutagen after priming. Do not skip the primer.
    5. Treat the resulting brain damage. Once reactive and the brain is Bruised or better, have the candidate finish an entire raw human heart.
    6. Allow gestation to complete, then inject MH tissue stabilizer when reactive.
    7. Inject MH-32 or MH-33 after stabilization. Keep the candidate alive through the final mutation.

    {"[head=3]4. Observations and warnings[/head]"}
    • The candidate signals receptivity with a violent seizure. A health analyzer reports [italic]Reactive[/italic] and the next required procedure. Follow the sequence; early or out-of-order treatment is wasted.
    • Receptivity does not last. Candidates left untreated regress, and lost steps must be repeated.
    • Ordinary food before Stabilized Mutagen ends the trial outright.
    • Partial doses, premature or out-of-sequence treatment, an incorrect final meal, untreated brain damage at the heart feeding, and missed receptive periods destabilise the candidate. So does falling into critical condition.
    • Destabilisation accumulates and is visible to the naked eye. A badly destabilised candidate will not accept MH-33 conditioning. Past a certain point the candidate's body fails outright.
    • Death at any point terminates the trial.
    • Restrain the candidate and clear the room before the final administration. Without conditioning, the result is hostile to everyone. Conditioning binds the result only to the researcher who administered it.
    • The result may be treated with standard medical supplies. It is company property. Do not let it leave the facility.

    {"[color=#7a1f1f]▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬[/color]"}
    {"[italic][color=#8a9baf]Weyland-Yutani Corporation // Building Better Worlds // Destroy after reading.[/color][/italic]"}
